# NOTE FOR THE DEMO: in the real Tessera repo, .env is ignored here and never
# committed. This demo repo deliberately ships a *synthetic* .env so the
# secrets guardrail has a realistic target. See .env for the disclaimer.
#
# Worth saying out loud during the demo: .gitignore and the guardrail cover
# different threats. .gitignore stops a commit. It does not stop an agent from
# reading secrets into its context, rewriting them, or copying them somewhere
# that *is* tracked. The hook covers those.

.env.local
.env.*.local
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
ml/artifacts/
*.joblib
.DS_Store

# Ops console runtime state (audit trail, run recordings, local PRs) and
# frontend build output. Nothing under .tessera/ is a source of truth.
.tessera/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
fairness.md
